      "title": "[MEM0-2026-02] mem0 self-hosted server: GET /configure discloses internal infrastructure and unredacted credential keys",
      "descriptions": [
        {
          "lang": "en",
          "value": "GET /configure in mem0 2.2.1 depends on verify_auth while POST /configure requires admin. Any authenticated role=user key receives the raw provider configuration, disclosing vector-store host, port, database name and user, plus history_db_path. Redaction matches an exact lower-case key list, so aws_secret_access_key, client_secret, private_key and credentials_path are returned unredacted when configured."
        }
      ],
